---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-05-03';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for seanreardon.com — what's collected, who it's shared with, how long it's kept, and your rights as a visitor."
  searchable={true}
>
  {/* `data-pagefind-body` scope-limits Pagefind's indexing to the article
      body — excludes nav/footer/page-title from the index. See BaseLayout's
      `searchable` prop docstring for the full corpus rule. */}
  <article class="privacy-policy" data-pagefind-body>
    <p class="last-updated"><strong>Last updated:</strong> {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This policy describes how <a href="https://seanreardon.com">seanreardon.com</a> — a personal
      portfolio and writing site operated by Sean Reardon — collects, uses, and discloses
      information about visitors. It applies to all interactions with the site, including
      reading content, submitting forms, and using interactive AI features when those
      eventually ship.
    </p>

    <p>
      The policy is written in plain language. If anything is unclear, <a href="/reach-out/">get in touch</a>
      and I'll clarify.
    </p>

    <h2>What you should know up front</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>No advertising. No tracking pixels. No third-party cookies. No marketing analytics.</li>
      <li>The site uses Cloudflare's privacy-respecting Web Analytics, which is <strong>cookieless</strong> and aggregates data without identifying individual visitors.</li>
      <li>The only personal information collected is what you voluntarily submit (email for newsletter, contact-form messages).</li>
      <li>I don't sell or share your personal information with anyone. There's no opt-out mechanism because there's nothing to opt out of.</li>
      <li>This is a personal portfolio site. Compliance work voluntarily exceeds what's strictly required at this scale because privacy practices are signal as much as obligation.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="what-is-collected">What data is collected</h2>

    <h3>From every visitor (passive collection)</h3>

    <p>
      <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> captures aggregate site usage:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Page views</li>
      <li>Country (geolocated from IP, then IP discarded)</li>
      <li>Browser type and operating system</li>
      <li>Referring website (where you clicked from, if any)</li>
      <li>Core Web Vitals (page load timing measurements)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This data is <strong>cookieless</strong>, contains <strong>no persistent identifiers</strong>,
      and cannot be tied back to individual visitors. No consent is required because no personal
      information is processed.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Apache server logs</strong> record HTTP requests for operational purposes (debugging,
      security auditing). Logs include IP addresses for the duration of the request and short-term
      log retention; IPs are not used for any tracking, profiling, or advertising purpose.
    </p>

    <h3>From you (active collection — only when you submit it)</h3>

    <p>
      <strong>Newsletter signup form</strong> collects:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Email address (required)</li>
      <li>First name (optional, for personalization)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Subscribers are managed in self-hosted Listmonk infrastructure on this site's own server.
      Newsletter delivery is handled by Resend (an external SMTP relay). You can unsubscribe via
      a one-click link in every email.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Contact form</strong> collects:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Name (first and last)</li>
      <li>Email address</li>
      <li>Website URL (optional)</li>
      <li>Your message</li>
      <li>Topic selector (general inquiry, privacy request, etc.)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Submissions are emailed to me directly and stored only as long as needed to respond
      (see retention table below).
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> runs in the background when you submit a form, to
      verify that you're not a bot. Turnstile is Cloudflare's privacy-respecting alternative to
      Google reCAPTCHA — it uses no fingerprinting in default mode and doesn't track you across
      sites. Cloudflare receives only the minimum metadata needed for the bot check.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Adobe Fonts</strong> serves one of the typefaces used on this site (Mostra Nuova,
      a display typeface used for large titles). When your browser loads a page, it makes a
      connection to Adobe's font CDN to retrieve the typeface. Adobe receives standard request
      metadata (your IP address, user-agent string, page referrer) for the duration of the
      request. Adobe Fonts does not set tracking cookies, does not fingerprint, and does not
      track you across sites. The site's other typefaces (Cardo, IBM Plex Sans, IBM Plex Mono)
      are self-hosted and do not involve a third-party connection.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>AI features (planned, not yet live):</strong> when AI-powered features ship on the
      site, your input may be sent to a language-model provider (primarily Anthropic). Each AI
      feature will explicitly disclose what's transmitted and request your consent at the point
      of use. Inputs and outputs are not retained on this site's servers unless strictly necessary
      for the feature.
    </p>

    <h2 id="processors">Third-party processors</h2>

    <p>
      Data is shared with these third parties, exclusively for the purposes listed:
    </p>

    <table class="processors">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Processor</th>
          <th>Data shared</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
          <th>Their privacy terms</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Cloudflare, Inc.</td>
          <td>Aggregate page-view counts; IP for geolocation (then discarded)</td>
          <td>CDN, edge security, web analytics, image hosting</td>
          <td><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="external nofollow noopener">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Resend Inc. (with Amazon SES underneath)</td>
          <td>Your email address; newsletter content</td>
          <td>Sending newsletter emails you've opted into</td>
          <td><a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="external nofollow noopener">resend.com/legal/privacy-policy</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Cloudflare (Turnstile)</td>
          <td>Minimal form-submission metadata for bot verification (no fingerprinting in default mode)</td>
          <td>Bot detection on form submissions</td>
          <td><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="external nofollow noopener">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Adobe Inc. (Adobe Fonts)</td>
          <td>IP address, user-agent, page referrer (per font request; no tracking cookies)</td>
          <td>Typeface delivery for site display (Mostra Nuova only; other typefaces self-hosted)</td>
          <td><a href="https://www.adobe.com/privacy/policy.html" rel="external nofollow noopener">adobe.com/privacy/policy</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Anthropic <em>(when AI features ship)</em></td>
          <td>Your input to specific AI features at the moment of use</td>
          <td>Generating AI responses you've explicitly invoked</td>
          <td><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" rel="external nofollow noopener">anthropic.com/legal/privacy</a></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
      No data is shared with advertisers, marketing networks, data brokers, or any party not
      listed above.
    </p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and similar technologies</h2>

    <p>
      This site uses <strong>no tracking cookies and no third-party cookies</strong>. The only
      cookies that may be set are strictly-necessary session cookies for form submissions (for
      example, Turnstile's verification token), and they expire when you close your browser.
    </p>

    <p>
      If a future feature requires a different category of cookies (analytics with persistent
      identifiers, marketing pixels, etc.), this policy will be updated and a consent banner
      will appear before any non-essential cookies are set.
    </p>

    <h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>

    <table class="retention">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Data category</th>
          <th>Retention period</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Cloudflare Web Analytics aggregates</td>
          <td>~6 months in CF dashboards (Cloudflare's default)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Apache server logs</td>
          <td>14 days, then purged</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Newsletter subscriber list</td>
          <td>Until you unsubscribe</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Contact form submissions</td>
          <td>90 days from receipt, then purged from server logs and inbox</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>AI feature inputs/outputs <em>(when shipped)</em></td>
          <td>Not retained on this site's servers</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
      You can request deletion of any data you've provided at any time — see <a href="#your-rights">Your rights</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights (GDPR — for EU/EEA visitors)</h2>

    <p>
      If you are in the European Union or European Economic Area, the General Data Protection
      Regulation gives you the following rights:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> — ask what personal data is held about you</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion</strong> — request that your data be deleted</li>
      <li><strong>Correction</strong> — request that inaccurate data be corrected</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong> — request a copy of your data in a machine-readable format</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction</strong> — request limits on how your data is processed</li>
      <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to specific processing activities</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — withdraw any consent you've previously given</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Cross-border transfers (data leaving the EU/EEA) are protected by Standard Contractual
      Clauses with all listed processors.
    </p>

    <p>
      To exercise any right, <a href="/reach-out/">use the contact form</a> with the "Privacy
      request" topic. I'll respond within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2 id="california-rights">California Privacy Rights</h2>

    <p>
      If you are a California resident, the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA) provides
      additional rights. This site is not a CPRA-covered business at its current scale — the
      law applies only above specific revenue and visitor thresholds — but I voluntarily honor
      the spirit of the law:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Right to know</strong> — what categories of personal information are collected, the sources, the purposes, and which third parties receive them. See <a href="#what-is-collected">What data is collected</a> and <a href="#processors">Third-party processors</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to delete</strong> — request deletion of personal information</li>
      <li><strong>Right to correct</strong> — request correction of inaccurate personal information</li>
      <li><strong>Right to opt out of sale/sharing</strong> — see <a href="#do-not-sell">Do Not Sell or Share</a> below</li>
      <li><strong>Right to limit use of sensitive personal information</strong> — this site does not collect sensitive personal information (no government IDs, financial account numbers, precise geolocation, biometrics, race/ethnicity/religion, health data, sexual orientation, etc.)</li>
      <li><strong>Non-discrimination</strong> — visitors who exercise rights receive the same service quality</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      To exercise California rights, <a href="/reach-out/">use the contact form</a> with the
      "Privacy request" topic and indicate your state. Response within 45 days per CPRA timing.
    </p>

    <h2 id="do-not-sell">Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>I do not sell or share your personal information.</strong>
    </p>

    <p>
      Cloudflare Web Analytics is aggregate-only and does not generate per-visitor data that
      could be sold. Newsletter subscribers are managed only on this site's self-hosted
      infrastructure — no third-party marketing list. Contact form submissions are received
      by me directly and not transmitted to any marketing or advertising network.
    </p>

    <p>
      There is therefore no opt-out mechanism needed for "sale or sharing" — there is nothing
      being sold or shared. This declarative statement is the affirmation of your right.
    </p>

    <p>
      If a future feature ever changes this stance (extremely unlikely for a personal
      portfolio), this policy will be updated and a functional opt-out mechanism added.
    </p>

    <h2 id="transfers">International data transfers</h2>

    <p>
      Some processors listed above (Cloudflare, Resend, Google, Anthropic) operate from the
      United States. When data crosses borders, transfers are protected by <strong>Standard
      Contractual Clauses</strong> (SCCs) per each provider's published policies. SCCs are the
      European Commission's approved mechanism for lawful cross-border data transfer.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">Children's privacy</h2>

    <p>
      This site is not directed to children under 13 (or 16 in some jurisdictions), and I do
      not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has
      provided personal information through this site, <a href="/reach-out/">contact me</a> and
      I'll delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ai-features">AI features (forward-looking)</h2>

    <p>
      Currently this site has no live AI features. When they ship:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Each feature will display a clear notice describing what's sent to which provider</li>
      <li>Anthropic will be the primary LLM provider; their commercial terms include no-training-on-user-data by default (your input does not train future models)</li>
      <li>AI feature consent will be requested at the point of feature invocation, not via a generic banner</li>
      <li>Inputs and outputs will not be retained on this site's servers unless strictly necessary for the feature</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>

    <p>
      Updates land at this same URL with a new "Last updated" date. Material changes will be
      flagged at the top of the policy for 30 days following the change so returning visitors
      can review.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>

    <p>
      For privacy questions, requests, or concerns:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Email: <a href="mailto:sean@seanreardon.com">sean@seanreardon.com</a></li>
      <li>Contact form: <a href="/reach-out/">/reach-out/</a> — use the "Privacy request" topic</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      For GDPR requests: response within 30 days. For California requests: response within
      45 days.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-policy {
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .last-updated {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .privacy-policy h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .privacy-policy h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }
  .privacy-policy table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-block: var(--space-md);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .privacy-policy th,
  .privacy-policy td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-sm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-muted);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .privacy-policy th {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .privacy-policy ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .privacy-policy ul li {
    margin-block: 0.25em;
  }
  .privacy-policy a {
    word-break: break-word;
  }
</style>
